text = "TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF SOFTWARE USAGE

Last Updated: Whenever the Captain remembers to update this page.

IMPORTANT NOTICE:

PLEASE READ THESE TERMS AND CONDITIONS CAREFULLY BEFORE INSTALLING, OPENING, CLICKING, DOUBLE-CLICKING, RIGHT-CLICKING, LEFT-CLICKING, THINKING ABOUT CLICKING, OR OTHERWISE INTERACTING WITH THIS SOFTWARE.

By pressing the \"I AGREE\", \"CONTINUE\", \"INSTALL\", \"ARRR, I ACCEPT\", or any button which appears to be related to continuing with the installation of this software, you hereby acknowledge that you have read, understood, misunderstood, ignored, skimmed, speed-read, or otherwise become aware of these Terms and Conditions.

If you do not agree to these Terms and Conditions, please close this installer immediately and return to whatever perfectly legitimate activity you were doing before finding this extremely questionable piece of software.

If you have already clicked \"I Agree\" without reading this document, congratulations. You have become part of the problem.

------------------------------------------------------------

1. DEFINITIONS

For the purposes of this Agreement:

\"THE SOFTWARE\" means the application you are currently attempting to install.

\"THE APPLICATION\" means the Software.

\"THIS PROGRAM\" means the Application.

\"THE THING\" means the Program.

\"THE PACKAGE\" means the collection of files you are about to place on your computer.

\"WE\", \"US\", \"OUR\", \"THE COMPANY\", \"THE DEVELOPERS\", \"THE PIRATES\", \"THE CREW\", \"THE CAPTAIN\", or \"THOSE GUYS WHO MADE THIS\" refers to the individuals responsible for creating this software.

\"YOU\" refers to the person currently staring at this Terms and Conditions window.

\"YOUR COMPUTER\" refers to the electronic device upon which you have chosen to install this software.

\"COMPUTER\" may also refer to your laptop, desktop, toaster with a graphics card, suspiciously powerful school computer, or other compatible computing apparatus.

\"EMULATION\" refers to the process by which software designed for one computing platform is reproduced or simulated on another computing platform.

\"EMULATOR\" refers to software which performs emulation.

\"USER\" refers to you.

\"CAPTAIN\" refers to whoever currently has the highest score, owns the server, wrote the most code, or is currently shouting the loudest.

\"PARROT\" refers to the theoretical bird that may or may not exist somewhere aboard the theoretical ship.

\"BOOTY\" means treasure. Please stop laughing.

------------------------------------------------------------

2. ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS

By installing or using the Software, you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions.

If you disagree with any portion of these Terms and Conditions, you may not use the Software.

If you disagree with only some of them, unfortunately there is no checkbox for that.

If you disagree with all of them, congratulations on maintaining your principles.

If you disagree with the Terms but click \"I Agree\" anyway, you have technically agreed to the Terms.

We are not responsible for the consequences of clicking buttons without reading what they do.

You may be asked to confirm your acceptance more than once.

This is not because we distrust you.

It is because we enjoy making buttons.

------------------------------------------------------------

3. THE SOFTWARE

The Software is provided as-is, as-was, as-will-be, and occasionally as-why-is-it-doing-that.

The Developers make no guarantee that the Software will:

- Work.
- Open.
- Close.
- Start.
- Finish.
- Stop.
- Recognize your controller.
- Recognize your keyboard.
- Recognize that one very specific button on your keyboard.
- Recognize your existence.
- Successfully emulate anything.
- Fail to emulate anything.
- Not crash.
- Crash in an entertaining manner.
- Save your progress.
- Remember your settings.
- Forget your settings.
- Behave normally.
- Behave abnormally.
- Behave at all.

The Developers shall not be held responsible for software behaving exactly as software sometimes behaves.

The Developers also make no promise that the Software will improve your life.

We actually make no promises about your life whatsoever.

------------------------------------------------------------

4. LICENSE

Subject to these Terms, you are granted a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to use the Software for its intended purpose.

You may install the Software on a compatible computer.

You may open the Software.

You may close the Software.

You may stare at the Software.

You may question why you installed the Software.

You may complain about the Software.

You may tell your friends about the Software.

You may not claim that you personally invented the Software unless you actually did.

You may not sell the Software and then become mysteriously surprised when we notice.

You may not put the Software inside a sandwich.

There is no reason for this last rule.

We simply felt it was necessary.

------------------------------------------------------------

5. SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS

The Software requires a computer.

We strongly recommend having a computer that is turned on.

Minimum system requirements may include:

Operating System: A reasonably modern operating system.

Processor: Something capable of processing instructions.

Memory: RAM.

Storage: Enough storage to store the Software.

Graphics: Something capable of displaying pixels.

Internet: Maybe.

Brain: Recommended.

Common Sense: Highly recommended.

A functioning computer: Mandatory.

A keyboard: Recommended.

A mouse: Also recommended.

A monitor: Surprisingly useful.

If your computer does not meet these requirements, the Software may operate slowly, quickly, sideways, diagonally, or not at all.

The Developers are not responsible if you attempt to install the Software on a calculator.

------------------------------------------------------------

6. EMULATION

The Software may contain features related to emulation.

Emulation is a complicated technical process involving computers pretending to be other computers.

This is perfectly normal.

Probably.

The Developers are not responsible if your computer suddenly becomes confused about which computer it is.

You agree not to blame the Software if your computer begins saying things such as:

\"I remember when I was a PlayStation.\"

We have no explanation for this.

We also cannot guarantee that the emulated platform will remember you.

------------------------------------------------------------

7. COMPATIBILITY

Not every game, program, file, or digital artifact is guaranteed to work with the Software.

Some files may:

- Work perfectly.
- Work poorly.
- Work upside down.
- Produce graphical glitches.
- Produce audio glitches.
- Produce absolutely nothing.
- Crash immediately.
- Crash eventually.
- Crash only when someone is watching.
- Work once and never again.
- Work after restarting the computer.
- Work after restarting the computer twice.
- Work for your friend but not for you.
- Work on Tuesday but mysteriously fail on Wednesday.

If a particular piece of software does not work, please do not repeatedly launch it 47 times expecting a different result.

Although we respect the determination.

------------------------------------------------------------

8. DOWNLOADS

The Software may provide functionality related to downloading files.

You are responsible for ensuring that you have the legal right to download and use any content you choose to download.

The Developers do not grant you ownership of any third-party content.

We provide tools.

What you do with those tools is your responsibility.

Please do not download things you are not legally allowed to download.

The Captain has spoken.

The Captain would also like to remind you that \"I found it on the internet\" is generally not considered a legal defense.

------------------------------------------------------------

9. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

All trademarks, logos, characters, names, sounds, images, software, and other intellectual property belonging to third parties remain the property of their respective owners.

The Developers do not claim ownership over third-party intellectual property.

If something belongs to somebody else, it belongs to somebody else.

This is a surprisingly difficult concept for pirates.

The Software itself, including its original code, artwork, interface, text, sounds, and other original materials, remains the property of the Developers unless otherwise stated.

Please do not steal our stuff while using our stuff to steal other stuff.

The irony would be unbearable.

------------------------------------------------------------

10. THE PIRATE CLAUSE

Despite the suspicious aesthetic of this application, the Developers would like to formally clarify that they are not actual pirates.

We do not own a ship.

We do not have a treasure chest.

We do not have a parrot.

We have not buried treasure.

If we had buried treasure, we would probably forget where we put it.

Any pirate imagery, pirate terminology, pirate references, pirate hats, pirate flags, pirate sounds, pirate jokes, or excessive use of the word \"ARRR\" are purely thematic.

ARRR.

------------------------------------------------------------

11. PIRATE TERMINOLOGY

The Software may contain phrases such as:

\"ARRR\"

\"MATEY\"

\"YE SCALLYWAG\"

\"WALK THE PLANK\"

\"AVAST\"

\"CAPTAIN\"

\"BOOTY\"

\"TREASURE\"

\"LAND AHOY\"

\"FULL SPEED AHEAD\"

These phrases are not intended to constitute actual maritime instructions.

If the Software tells you to \"walk the plank\", do not walk a plank.

If the Software tells you to \"abandon ship\", first determine whether there is actually a ship.

If there is no ship, please remain where you are.

------------------------------------------------------------

12. ADVERTISEMENTS

The Software may display advertisements.

These advertisements may appear:

- At inconvenient times.
- In inconvenient places.
- Slightly too close to important buttons.
- Suspiciously close to the button you intended to press.
- With an X button approximately the size of an atom.
- Immediately after you successfully close another advertisement.
- At the exact moment you were about to click something important.

The Developers are not responsible for your inability to locate an advertisement's close button.

The Developers are also not responsible if you accidentally click an advertisement because the close button was approximately three pixels away from where you thought it was.

This is called user interface design.

Probably.

------------------------------------------------------------

13. POPUPS

You acknowledge that popup windows may appear during certain operations.

You agree not to become emotionally attached to them.

You also agree not to name them.

The Developers specifically reject responsibility for any relationship formed between the user and a popup window.

Popups are temporary.

Popups are annoying.

Popups are inevitable.

Popups are watching.

Actually, no.

We are legally required to clarify that the popups are not watching you.

Probably.

If a popup appears and you close it, another popup may appear.

This is not a bug.

It is a lifestyle.

------------------------------------------------------------

14. PERFORMANCE

The Software may consume system resources.

This may include:

- RAM.
- CPU.
- GPU.
- Storage.
- Battery.
- Internet bandwidth.
- Patience.
- Sanity.
- Your willingness to continue reading these Terms.

The Developers shall not be responsible for any reduction in available RAM caused by the Software.

If the Software displays:

ERROR: NOT ENOUGH RAM

please remain calm.

Your RAM may be completely fine.

The Software may simply be dramatic.

If your computer begins making concerning noises, please investigate whether the noise is coming from the computer before blaming us.

------------------------------------------------------------

15. DATA

The Developers do not guarantee that your data will be preserved.

You should maintain backups of important files.

Do not store the only copy of your extremely important school project inside a folder named:

DO_NOT_DELETE_FINAL_FINAL_REAL_FINAL_2

We know what you are doing.

Back it up.

Seriously.

We are not responsible for your decision to store irreplaceable files next to a suspicious executable called \"totally_safe_final.exe\".

------------------------------------------------------------

16. SAVE FILES

Save files may become corrupted.

Save files may disappear.

Save files may refuse to load.

Save files may load but contain absolutely nothing useful.

Save files may mysteriously become significantly larger than expected.

If this happens, we recommend remaining calm and checking your backups.

If you do not have backups, we recommend learning from the experience.

If you lose 40 hours of progress and have no backup, we recommend staring silently at the wall for approximately six minutes before doing anything else.

------------------------------------------------------------

17. SECURITY

You are responsible for maintaining reasonable security practices on your computer.

Do not install suspicious files.

Do not open suspicious attachments.

Do not trust suspicious websites.

Do not enter your password into a website called:

FREE-MONEY-NO-SCAM-REAL.COM

If you do this anyway, we cannot help you.

We warned you.

If a stranger offers you free cryptocurrency in exchange for your password, that is probably not a good deal.

------------------------------------------------------------

18. PASSWORDS

The Developers will never ask you for your password through this Terms and Conditions window.

If this Terms and Conditions window asks for your password:

DO NOT ENTER IT.

If the Terms and Conditions window starts asking for your mother's maiden name:

CLOSE THE PROGRAM.

If it asks for your social security number:

WHY ARE YOU STILL HERE?

If it asks for your blood type:

SOMETHING HAS GONE VERY WRONG.

------------------------------------------------------------

19. COOKIES

The Software may use cookies, metaphorical cookies, digital cookies, or no cookies whatsoever.

Despite what the word \"cookie\" may suggest, the Software does not provide snacks.

If cookies are present, please do not attempt to eat them.

If you find an actual cookie inside your computer, please remove it immediately.

Do not attempt to install it.

------------------------------------------------------------

20. INTERNET CONNECTION

Certain features may require an internet connection.

The Developers cannot control:

- Your internet service provider.
- Your router.
- Your Wi-Fi.
- Your Ethernet cable.
- Your neighbor's Wi-Fi.
- The weather.
- The mysterious outage affecting only your house.

If the internet stops working, please verify that your router is connected before blaming the Software.

If restarting the router fixes the problem, please pretend you knew that was the solution all along.

------------------------------------------------------------

21. HARDWARE

The Developers are not responsible for hardware damage caused by misuse, overheating, improper installation, anger, rage, frustration, throwing the computer, or attempting to \"fix\" the computer with a hammer.

A hammer is not a troubleshooting tool.

We cannot believe we had to write that.

Do not hit the computer.

The computer is innocent.

------------------------------------------------------------

22. BUGS

The Software may contain bugs.

Some bugs may be known.

Some bugs may be unknown.

Some bugs may be features.

Some features may be bugs.

Some bugs may become features.

Some features may become bugs after an update.

If you discover a bug, congratulations.

You have discovered something we probably forgot about.

If the bug is particularly impressive, please report it.

If the bug is hilarious, please also report it.

If the bug causes the entire screen to turn purple and display the word \"BANANA\", definitely report it.

------------------------------------------------------------

23. UPDATES

The Developers may release updates from time to time.

Updates may:

- Fix bugs.
- Add bugs.
- Remove bugs.
- Add features.
- Remove features.
- Change things.
- Break things.
- Make things better.
- Make things worse.
- Make things different.
- Move buttons.
- Rename buttons.
- Make buttons slightly larger.
- Make buttons slightly smaller for no reason.

The Developers reserve the right to update the Software without asking whether you are emotionally prepared for the update.

------------------------------------------------------------

24. INSTALLATION

During installation, the Software may display progress indicators.

These indicators may or may not represent actual progress.

If the installer reaches 99% and remains there for an unusually long period of time, please remain patient.

If it reaches 100% and remains there forever, please remain slightly less patient.

If the installer says \"Installation Complete\" but the program does not appear to exist, congratulations.

You have successfully installed something.

We think.

------------------------------------------------------------

25. UNINSTALLATION

You may uninstall the Software at any time.

The Developers encourage users to use the official uninstaller where available.

Please do not delete random files from your computer and hope for the best.

If you accidentally delete System32, we cannot help you.

We really cannot help you.

Please stop.

------------------------------------------------------------

26. TECHNICAL SUPPORT

Technical support may be provided depending on availability.

Before requesting support, please attempt the following:

1. Close the Software.
2. Open the Software again.
3. Restart your computer.
4. Check whether your computer is actually turned on.
5. Check whether the monitor is turned on.
6. Check whether the monitor is plugged in.
7. Check whether the keyboard is plugged in.
8. Check whether you accidentally turned the volume down.
9. Check whether you are actually using the correct application.
10. Question your life choices.

If none of these work, contact support.

------------------------------------------------------------

27. USER CONDUCT

You agree not to use the Software for unlawful purposes.

You agree not to intentionally damage the Software.

You agree not to attempt to crash the Software.

You agree not to summon supernatural entities through the Software.

You agree not to install the Software on a submarine.

Unless the submarine has Windows.

Then maybe.

You also agree not to use the Software to annoy your friends more than is socially acceptable.

There is, unfortunately, no objective measurement for this.

Use your judgment.

------------------------------------------------------------

28. THE SUBMARINE CLAUSE

The Developers make absolutely no guarantees regarding submarine compatibility.

If you are currently reading these Terms and Conditions from inside a submarine, please contact your commanding officer.

We have questions.

Why are you installing this on a submarine?

Who gave you Wi-Fi?

Is the Captain aware?

------------------------------------------------------------

29. AIRCRAFT COMPATIBILITY

The Developers also make no guarantees regarding aircraft compatibility.

Please do not attempt to troubleshoot the Software while piloting an aircraft.

Please do not install updates during takeoff.

Please do not ask the pilot to \"just restart it.\"

We are begging you.

------------------------------------------------------------

30. REFUNDS

If the Software was obtained for free, there is nothing to refund.

If you somehow paid money for this Software without us knowing about it, please contact whoever charged you.

We have no idea how you managed that.

If you paid someone three hundred dollars for this free application, please reconsider your financial decision-making process.

------------------------------------------------------------

31. MODIFICATIONS

You may not modify, reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise tamper with the Software except where such activities are permitted by applicable law.

If you modify the Software anyway and it explodes:

That is between you and the Software.

We were not there.

We saw nothing.

We know nothing.

The parrot knows nothing.

------------------------------------------------------------

32. STREAMING AND RECORDING

You may record gameplay or other interactions with the Software for personal or entertainment purposes, subject to applicable laws and the rights of third parties.

If you upload a video of yourself becoming increasingly frustrated with the Software, we will probably watch it.

If the video gets a million views, we will pretend we planned that.

------------------------------------------------------------

33. SPEEDRUNNING

Speedrunning the Software is permitted.

However, the Developers accept no responsibility for:

- Extremely fast clicking.
- Broken keyboards.
- Broken mice.
- Broken world records.
- Emotional damage.
- Carpal tunnel.
- Screaming.
- Friends asking why you are doing this.

If you discover a sequence that allows you to finish the entire application in three seconds, please report it.

Unless it is really funny.

Then send us the video first.

------------------------------------------------------------

34. THE CAPTAIN'S DECISION

In any situation not explicitly covered by these Terms and Conditions, the final decision shall be made by the Captain.

The Captain may be:

- A developer.
- A moderator.
- A particularly confident player.
- A random person named Steve.
- Nobody.

The Developers reserve the right to appoint a Captain at any time.

The Captain may not actually have legal authority.

This clause is mostly for decoration.

------------------------------------------------------------

35. THE PARROT

The parrot has no authority over this Agreement.

The parrot cannot approve your installation.

The parrot cannot reject your installation.

The parrot cannot provide technical support.

The parrot cannot legally represent the Developers.

The parrot cannot be held liable for anything.

The parrot may, however, be extremely loud.

------------------------------------------------------------

36. TREASURE

Any reference to treasure contained within the Software is fictional unless otherwise explicitly stated.

The Developers do not guarantee the existence of:

- Gold.
- Diamonds.
- Ancient artifacts.
- Secret maps.
- Buried treasure.
- Hidden chests.
- Magical swords.
- Islands.
- Cursed necklaces.
- Legendary pirate booty.

If you find actual treasure while using the Software, please contact the Developers immediately.

Actually, don't.

Keep it.

We have changed our minds.

------------------------------------------------------------

37. USER PRIVACY

The Developers respect user privacy.

The Software should not be interpreted as granting the Developers unlimited access to your computer.

The Developers do not need to know what is inside your Downloads folder.

We do not want to know.

We especially do not want to know why there are 47 copies of the same file.

Clean your Downloads folder.

------------------------------------------------------------

38. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES

The Software may interact with third-party services.

Third-party services are controlled by their respective operators.

The Developers cannot guarantee that third-party services will remain available.

If a third-party service disappears overnight, please do not blame the Software.

If a website changes its layout and everything breaks, please do not blame the Software.

Actually, you can blame the Software a little.

------------------------------------------------------------

39. COMPATIBILITY WITH OTHER SOFTWARE

The Software may interact poorly with other applications.

Possible conflicts may include:

- Antivirus software.
- Firewalls.
- Overlays.
- Screen recorders.
- Game launchers.
- Voice chat programs.
- RGB lighting software.
- Extremely aggressive calculator applications.

If your RGB keyboard stops glowing because of this Software, please remain calm.

Your keyboard is still a keyboard.

It simply has fewer lights.

------------------------------------------------------------

40. BATTERY LIFE

If you use the Software on a laptop, battery life may decrease.

This is because computers require electricity.

This is not a revolutionary discovery.

The Developers are not responsible if you begin the Software at 100% battery and finish at 2%.

Please bring your charger.

------------------------------------------------------------

41. WEATHER

The Software does not control the weather.

If it rains while you are installing the Software, this is a coincidence.

If it stops raining after you close the Software, this is also a coincidence.

If it starts raining whenever you open the Software, we recommend investigating your local weather patterns.

------------------------------------------------------------

42. TIME

The Developers are not responsible for time lost while using the Software.

If you begin playing at 8:00 PM and suddenly realize it is 3:00 AM, this is between you and your clock.

Please sleep.

Seriously.

------------------------------------------------------------

43. FOOD

Do not eat while operating the Software if doing so causes you to spill food on your keyboard.

The Developers are not responsible for:

- Soda damage.
- Pizza damage.
- Crumb damage.
- Sauce damage.
- Coffee damage.
- Mysterious sticky key damage.

Keep your food away from your electronics.

Your keyboard does not need dinner.

------------------------------------------------------------

44. EMOTIONAL DAMAGE

The Developers are not responsible for emotional damage caused by:

- Losing progress.
- Missing an important button.
- Getting defeated.
- Failing a challenge.
- Accidentally clicking something.
- Seeing an advertisement.
- Seeing another advertisement.
- Seeing the third advertisement.
- Realizing there are five more advertisements.

If the Software causes you to yell \"NOOOOOOO\", that is unfortunate.

But also slightly entertaining.

------------------------------------------------------------

45. SOUND

The Software may produce sounds.

These sounds may include:

- Music.
- Effects.
- Notifications.
- Alerts.
- Clicks.
- Beeps.
- Boops.
- Unexpected noises.

Please adjust the volume appropriately.

Do not blame the Developers if you open the Software at full volume in a quiet classroom.

You have been warned.

------------------------------------------------------------

46. CLASSROOM USE

The Developers do not recommend running the Software during important classes.

If your teacher asks why your computer is displaying eight suspicious advertisements and a pirate website, please do not say:

\"The Terms and Conditions told me to.\"

They did not.

------------------------------------------------------------

47. SCHOOL COMPUTERS

If you are using a school-owned computer, make sure you have permission to install software.

Do not attempt to bypass administrative restrictions.

Do not attempt to become the administrator.

Do not rename yourself \"Administrator\" and assume this makes you the administrator.

It does not.

We admire the confidence, however.

------------------------------------------------------------

48. LEGAL COMPLIANCE

You are responsible for complying with all applicable laws and regulations when using the Software.

The Developers do not encourage illegal activity.

The Developers do not provide legal advice.

The Developers do not know the laws of every country.

The Captain barely knows the laws of this ship.

------------------------------------------------------------

49. INTERNATIONAL USERS

The Software may be used by people from many different places.

Local laws may differ.

Some things that are permitted in one country may not be permitted in another.

Please investigate your local laws if you are unsure.

Do not ask the parrot.

The parrot has no idea.

------------------------------------------------------------

50. TERMINATION

You may stop using the Software at any time.

Simply uninstall it.

The Software will not chase you.

The Software will not send someone to your house.

The Software will not hide under your bed.

The Software will not steal your socks.

We promise.

If you uninstall the Software, we will respect your decision.

We may be sad.

But we will respect it.

------------------------------------------------------------

51. ACCEPTABLE USE

You agree to use the Software in a reasonable manner.

What constitutes \"reasonable\" is intentionally vague.

If you are doing something and think:

\"Surely nobody intended me to do this.\"

You are probably correct.

------------------------------------------------------------

52. FORBIDDEN ACTIVITIES

You may not use the Software to:

- Break the law.
- Harm other people.
- Damage other computers.
- Distribute malicious software.
- Harass others.
- Pretend to be the Developers.
- Pretend to be the Captain.
- Pretend to be the parrot.
- Claim the parrot wrote the Software.
- Attempt to marry the parrot.

The final rule was added after an incident.

We will not discuss the incident.

------------------------------------------------------------

53. BACKUPS

You are strongly encouraged to maintain backups.

A backup is a copy of important information stored somewhere other than the original location.

For example:

Computer → Backup Drive

is good.

Computer → Another folder on the same computer

is less good.

Computer → \"I'll remember it\"

is not a backup.

Your memory is not cloud storage.

------------------------------------------------------------

54. CLOUD STORAGE

Cloud storage is not actually stored inside clouds.

We feel this clarification is important.

The files are stored on physical computers somewhere.

Please do not attempt to retrieve them by looking into the sky.

------------------------------------------------------------

55. SUPPORT HOURS

Technical support hours may vary.

If nobody responds to your message at 3:47 AM, please understand that the Developers may be asleep.

If nobody responds at 3:47 PM, they may also be asleep.

Developers require sleep.

Sometimes.

------------------------------------------------------------

56. DOCUMENTATION

Documentation may contain errors.

If the documentation says:

\"Click the red button.\"

and the button is blue:

Please click the button that looks like the button we described.

If there is no button:

We apologize.

------------------------------------------------------------

57. FUTURE FEATURES

The Developers may discuss future features.

Future features are not guaranteed.

If we say:

\"Maybe we'll add multiplayer.\"

that does not mean multiplayer will be added.

If we say:

\"Multiplayer coming soon.\"

that means we probably have no idea when multiplayer is coming.

If we say:

\"Multiplayer is finished.\"

then congratulations.

------------------------------------------------------------

58. RANDOMNESS

Certain parts of the Software may contain random behavior.

This randomness may cause events to happen in different orders.

If something happens twice in a row, it may still be random.

If something happens 37 times in a row, we may have accidentally written the code incorrectly.

Please report this.

------------------------------------------------------------

59. THE GOLDEN RULE OF TROUBLESHOOTING

When something goes wrong:

Do not panic.

Do not hit the computer.

Do not throw the computer.

Do not yell at the computer.

Do not threaten the computer.

The computer cannot understand you.

Probably.

Instead:

1. Read the error message.
2. Restart the application.
3. Check the documentation.
4. Restart the computer.
5. Ask for help.
6. Accept that sometimes computers are weird.

------------------------------------------------------------

60. FINAL DISCLAIMER

This Software is provided for entertainment and fictional purposes.

Nothing contained within this Agreement should be interpreted as legal advice.

The Developers are not lawyers.

The Captain is definitely not a lawyer.

The parrot is also not a lawyer.

The parrot has not completed law school.

Do not ask the parrot for legal advice.

------------------------------------------------------------

61. ACKNOWLEDGEMENT

By clicking \"I AGREE\", you acknowledge that:

- You have read these Terms.
- You understand these Terms.
- You probably didn't read these Terms.
- You are currently scrolling through a very long textbox.
- You have wondered how much longer this document is.
- You have probably considered clicking \"I Agree\" without finishing.
- We knew you would do this.
- You have reached a considerable distance into this document.
- You deserve a small break.
- There is still more.

Nevertheless, you are hereby considered to have been informed.

------------------------------------------------------------

62. FINAL FINAL DISCLAIMER

By continuing, you confirm that you are sufficiently confident in your decision to install this questionable software.

You accept responsibility for your own decisions.

You acknowledge that computers are complicated.

You acknowledge that pirates are fictional.

You acknowledge that the installer is probably fine.

Probably.

You acknowledge that clicking \"I AGREE\" is your own decision.

You acknowledge that you could have stopped reading approximately 1,500 words ago.

You didn't.

Respect.

------------------------------------------------------------

63. THE ABSOLUTELY FINAL DISCLAIMER

This is the final disclaimer.

Probably.

If another disclaimer appears below this one, then this was not actually the final disclaimer.

We apologize for the confusion.

Legal documents are complicated.

Pirate legal documents are considerably worse.

------------------------------------------------------------

64. AGREEMENT TO STOP READING

At this point, you have read enough.

You are permitted to stop.

You may scroll to the bottom.

Nobody will know.

Except the scrollbar.

The scrollbar knows everything.

------------------------------------------------------------

65. ACCEPTANCE

If you agree to these Terms and Conditions, click:

I AGREE

If you do not agree:

I DO NOT AGREE

If you are unsure:

Ask the Captain.

If the Captain is unavailable:

Ask the parrot.

If the parrot is unavailable:

Ask nobody.

If nobody is available:

Use your best judgment.

If your best judgment is unavailable:

Please restart your computer.

------------------------------------------------------------

66. THE CAPTAIN'S FINAL STATEMENT

The Captain has reviewed this document.

The Captain has decided that it is sufficiently long.

The Captain would like you to stop reading.

The Captain would like you to install the software.

The Captain would also like a sandwich.

Nobody knows why.

------------------------------------------------------------

67. FINAL FINAL FINAL ACCEPTANCE

By pressing the acceptance button, you confirm that you have read, understood, ignored, skimmed, or otherwise encountered these Terms and Conditions.

You agree to use the Software responsibly.

You agree not to blame the Developers for things clearly caused by you.

You agree not to blame the parrot.

You agree not to blame the Captain.

You agree not to blame the ship.

There is no ship.

------------------------------------------------------------

END OF TERMS AND CONDITIONS

Thank you for reading.

Seriously.

Thank you.

You made it.

ARRR.

Now install the thing.

Please.

We have been waiting here for a very long time."
